    {
      "name": "setup_concepts",
      "description": "Set up a repository, or change where diagrams are saved and how much each commit saves. Call it with no choices: the user gets a picker (where: this project docs/concepts/, their learning library ~/ConceptLibrary/<repo>/, or both; then per folder: Diagram (svg only, recommended), Editable (+ .excalidraw), Diagram + notes (+ README and concept notes), or Custom). If the client can't show it, this returns the questions for you to ask with your own multiple-choice tool; then call again with `destinations`. Changes apply to new commits; files already saved stay where they are. Writes .concepts.json (or the gitignored .concepts.local.json for scope \"personal\"), adds the workflow to AGENTS.md (and an @AGENTS.md import to CLAUDE.md for Claude Code), and optionally a post-commit reminder hook.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
